What:           /sys/class/power_supply/battery/device/soc_state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        moe-takasaki <199255379+moe-takasaki@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
                Linux-owned gauge persistence snapshot, not Android SDAM.
                Format: version unix_seconds charge_uah compensated_ocv_uv full
                hold_percent reason. Version2 adds the last two fields.
                hold_percent is -1 when active, otherwise0..100 at completion.
                reason:0 active,1 full,2 premature termination,3 voltage guard,
                4 user-target completion. Version1 non-full snapshots migrate;
                version1 full anchors are rejected as stale.
                Only sustained independently measured taper establishes full.
                 Reads are coherent under the gauge mutex.
                A root write restores once, only within 60 seconds of probe,
                with age <= 1 hour, valid charge/voltage bounds and an OCV
                difference <= 150 mV. full is 0/1 and accepted only near full.
                Intended for lunar-power-state, which saves on /data atomically.
                ADC calibration and Android battery state are never written.

What:           /sys/class/power_supply/battery/device/gauge_diagnostics
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        moe-takasaki <199255379+moe-takasaki@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
                FIFO event/error counts, persistence restore flag, compensated
                OCV, modeled impedance, thermal block, last policy error and
                source-current cap. An error count identifies missing coverage;
                it must not be interpreted as a validated charge measurement.

What:           /sys/class/power_supply/battery/device/charger_safety_test
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        moe-takasaki <199255379+moe-takasaki@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
                Root writes 1 during normal 15..40 C charging to test the real
                hard JEITA comparator. Temporarily lowers the hot cutoff below
                measured temperature, waits at most 5 seconds for hot status and
                disabled trickle/precharge/full-on charge modes,
                and always restores the production 45 C cutoff. No temperature
                limit is raised. Reads: 0 not run, 1 passed, negative errno failed.

What:           /sys/class/power_supply/battery/device/charge_end
Date:           October2026
Contact:        moe-takasaki <199255379+moe-takasaki@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
                Completion hold, starting percentage, validated-full flag,
                reason code (as above), last hardware charger state, measured
                taper duration and programmed recharge voltage. Read only.
                Every hardware termination holds charging off. A minute of
                measured10..200 mA current near the normal FV is required to
                anchor100%. A lower user FV completes without a full anchor.
                Restart needs5 percentage points of counted discharge plus
                30 s of low current and voltage below the recharge threshold.
                Near-full SOC>=90% caps requested cell current to500 mA.
